(-2) ONE WILL LOSE POINTS FOR EVERY DEPARTURE FROM THESE RULES.

(-1) ONE MUST use a RULER or appropriate software for every straight-line s=
egment UNLESS explicitly exempted in the list on the top sheet of the exam.=
 The lines must be VISIBLY STRAIGHT. When in doubt, use a ruler. Matrix bra=
ckets, conclusion bars, separating lines must be VISIBLY STRAIGHT. (-1 for =
every departure)

(0) Please upload a SINGLE DOCUMENT in pdf form. (One will have to resubmit=
 otherwise and you will lose 10 points the first time, 20 points the second=
 time and so on in arithmentic progression) The document should be less tha=
n or equal to 25 MB in size. Please reduce the resolution.



(1) Please fill in the top-sheet with the actual numerical values of parts =
and add the score along the rows and along the column. (-1 for every depart=
ure)

(2) Please add up the values for parts to get the total on a question and r=
ecord it on the same row; it may exceed 6 (-1 for every departure)



(3) Please add up all the values to get a total in the rectangle immediatel=
y to the left of TOTAL.(-1 otherwise)



(4) The notes contain examples worked out in detail with remarks about whic=
h aspects must be done differently on exams; one may NOT alter the formatti=
ng that one sees in these examples in any manner whatsoever. Please refer t=
o the Solved Exams.



(5) Please keep a 5 mm gap between the column of equalities on the left and=
 the expressions that they relate; this is done systematically in the notes=
 and it makes things much easier to check and recheck, than if they were pi=
led on top of each other with no attention to relative location as is often=
 the case on many exams.



(6) Every symbol has a specific meaning and should be read (in one of sever=
al ways) to produce a grammatically correct sentence that corresponds to th=
e sequence of symbols; some of this is explicitly written down in Sets Note=
s and you have to acquire the habit of always doing so.



(7) One must read the notes over and over to assimilate the material.



(8) One must read the Error file over and over to avoid the errors listed.



(9) One must prove every claim that you make  and check every answer that o=
ne writes.



(10) Please do NOT submit invented notation, improper formats, improper org=
anisation, or complete nonsense. (SEVERE PENALTIES)



(11) After exams are returned, if one wishes to respond to a comment, ONE M=
UST DO SO BY EMAIL IN CANVAS. Do not make a remark on the exam even though =
I will do so. YOne will need to download the exam to see these remarks. DO =
NOT WRITE REMARKS ON THE EXAM BUT SEND AN EMAIL within CANVAS.



(12) Do not make extraneous marks or sentences on any page, such as 'rest o=
n next page', 'PTO', or 'continued' because one will lose points. (-1 for e=
very departure)



(13) One must check one's work very carefully before submitting.



(14) NO DOT FOR MULTIPLICATION. Use juxtaposition or parentheses.



(15) NO DECIMALS unless the question requires it.



(16) ONE MAY ASK ME QUESTIONS ABOUT ONE'S GRADED EXAM ONLY AFTER I ANNOUNCE=
 THAT ONE MAY DO SO. (-5 for every departure)

